$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 SUM {
  coords 7070.548 152.503 742.933
  m_sTitle "Summary"
  m_sTextData "A British platoon must defend CIMIC House against a large-scale Iraqi assault aimed at overrunning and capturing the compound."\
  "Can the garrison hold long enough to force the attackers to withdraw?"\
  ""\
  "<h2>Summary Notes</h2>"\
  "• E-tool usage is strictly forbidden."\
  "• Iraqi forces only to be slotted if missions is <b>FULL</b> or if blufor accept the challenge."\
  "• The mission is <b>LIVE</b> from the moment you enter the game."\
  ""\
  "- This mission is the first in a series following a British regiment throughout its deployment in Kuwait during the 1991 Gulf War, known to the British as <b>Operation Granby</b> and to the Americans as <b>Operation Desert Storm</b>."\
  "Each mission is numbered sequentially using the <b>KD</b> prefix, meaning <b>Kuwait Days</b>, followed by the instalment number."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
 }
 MN {
  coords 7070.548 152.503 742.933
  m_sTitle "Mission notes"
  m_sTextData "<h2>GM Notes</h2>"\
  "We rarely run COOP defence missions. This scenario is intended to test the server under sustained defensive gameplay, with players holding a fixed position against continuous enemy assaults."\
  ""\
  "If, at any point, the server is struggling or the assault feels too weak or too strong, GMs are encouraged to adjust enemy numbers and pacing accordingly."\
  ""\
  "• You are restricted to Iraqi 2000 infantry."\
  "• You may spawn <b>ONE</b> UAZ PKM, BTR, BRDM, and BMP each. A maximum of one vehicle type may be active at any one time.~"\
  "(No more than two vehicles at one time)"\
  ""\
  "<h2>End Conditions</h2>"\
  "<b>British Victory:</b>"\
  "• Hold off the Iraqi assault for 30 minutes."\
  ""\
  "<b>Iraqi Victory:</b>"\
  "• Overrun the British garrison by eliminating at least 85% (26/30) of British forces and occupy the compound."\
  ""\
  "<h2>Mission Notes</h2>"\
  "• E-tool usage is strictly forbidden."\
  "• Iraqi forces only to be slotted if missions is <b>FULL</b> or if blufor accept the challenge."\
  "• JIP TP."\
  "• UK AO limit."\
  ""\
  "- This mission is the first in a series following a British regiment throughout its deployment in Kuwait during the 1991 Gulf War, known to the British as <b>Operation Granby</b> and to the Americans as <b>Operation Desert Storm</b>."\
  "Each mission is numbered sequentially using the <b>KD</b> prefix, meaning <b>Kuwait Days</b>, followed by the instalment number."\
  ""\
  "Mission made by TheLocalPub. Please use the <b>#feedback</b> channel on Discord to report issues or submit suggestions."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 10
 }
 CL {
  coords 7070.548 152.503 742.933
  m_sTitle "Changelog"
  m_sTextData "<h2>Added:</h2>"\
  "• More buildings around the outside of the compound and their respective markers."\
  "• Further low/small cover to the area outside the compound to make the AI not a total turkey shoot at times."\
  "• Further fortifications to the compound, including a ladder to the garage roof with fighting positions."\
  "• UK AO limit to brief."\
  "• MMG Markers"\
  ""\
  "<h2>Changed:</h2>"\
  "• AI settings - They should now be more aggressive, faster to the compound, and also better at engaging from a distance."\
  "• AI numbers - Increased by 10 units a wave."\
  "• AI placement - Moved some groups to different areas to try spread out their direction of travel."
  m_bEmptyFactionVisibility 1
  m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  m_iOrder 11
 }
}